# --- Project artefacts (regenerated, never tracked) ---
# Root-anchored: a bare `data/` would also match src/bkrobust/data/.
/results/*
!/results/.gitkeep
# The breakdown-radius demonstration's outputs ARE deliverables: report.md
# cites them and they are small CSV/JSON. Everything else under results/ is
# regenerated experiment output and stays untracked.
!/results/breakdown_radius_demo/
# Axis A / Axis B session outputs are deliverables too: the pre-registration,
# per-instance rows and manifests are cited by report_synth_and_search.md.
!/results/synth/
!/results/search/
# Session 2 (Axis B deep) outputs are deliverables cited by
# report_axisb_deep.md and THEOREMS.md.
!/results/axisb2/
!/results/axisb3/
!/results/axisb4/
!/results/axisa2/
!/results/axisa3/
# Axis Robustness (survival curves + Pareto frontier) outputs are deliverables
# cited by report_fragility_and_pareto.md; the pre-registration lives here too.
!/results/axis_robustness/
# Stage 0 of the evaluation plan: the claim-unit radius audit of the committed
# axisa3 rows, cited by docs/EVALUATION_PLAN.md and docs/PAPER_NARRATIVE.md.
!/results/stage0/
# Session 8 (the epsilon-bias radius) outputs are deliverables: every number in
# report_r_epsilon.md, docs/PAPER_INTEGRATION_R_EPSILON.md and
# paper/sections/epsilon-radius.tex traces to a file here, and the
# counterexample witnesses carry the SEMs needed to replay them. 936 KB total.
!/results/epsilon/
# The LLM background-knowledge elicitation (ported from ze/experiments): the
# frozen frame, questionnaire, per-condition answers and the knowledge sets K
# that the final table is computed at. The answer cache under
# results/elicit/cache/ stays untracked -- it regenerates in seconds from the
# committed remote answers via elicit_import.py.
!/results/frame/
!/results/elicit/
/results/elicit/cache/
# The final table: r_val and r_eps for every real network at its LLM-elicited
# K, per-instance rows plus the aggregate cited in the paper's results table.
!/results/final_table/
# The epsilon > 1 re-run of the final table (docs/RESULT_EPSILON_ABOVE_ONE.md):
# same schema as final_table, plus the per-instance staircase beta_up(d) and
# ceiling B(Chat) that make any future epsilon a lookup rather than a re-run.
!/results/final_table_eps_gt1/
# The exhaustive mean-vs-max shell study (docs/EXPERIMENT_MEAN_VS_MAX.md):
# every retraction state of 15 instances, with the full distribution of B per
# shell. Evidence for the shell-aggregation design decision.
!/results/mean_vs_max/
